  "evidence": "Read the concrete SPU/SWhit and Stokes suppliers, the weighted insertion and its homotopy, the signed group/affine-simplex telescoping proof, pairing with bar cycles, overlaps and the moving-frame majoration. The one-dimensional example checks the orientation in an explicit linear group action.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "CFM-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A partition contracts the group differential and produces a closed form",
      "anchor": "inputs-cocycle-differentials",
      "statement": "For a left-invariant homogeneous degree-m cocycle and the selected smooth partition, the recursion η₀=c, η_{j+1}=dKη_j preserves vanishing of the group coboundary and gives a closed smooth top form on the positive cone, independent of the remaining group argument.",
      "hypotheses": "Positive degree m=k+1. The abstract construction works on an open convex real domain preserved by the specified linear group action. The action translates a smooth function φ to locally finite weights which sum to 1. Arithmetic invariance of the resulting form also uses equivariance of the translates and diagonal invariance of the input cocycle.",
      "definitions": [
        "ψ_γ(h)=φ(A_{γ⁻¹}h), where A is the arithmetic action on the Hermitian matrices.",
        "δ deletes one group argument with alternating signs. K first inserts γ and sums against ψ_γ at h. The exterior differential d differentiates in h.",
        "At j form degree is j and group degree m−j, so at j=m only one group argument remains."
      ],
