      "title": "Stokes moves the remaining group faces to the simplex boundary",
      "anchor": "inputs-cocycle-stokes",
      "statement": "The signed substitution δB_j=W_j+(−1)^(m−1−j)W_{j+1} yields c=δb+sW_m as homogeneous cochains. In degree m the form ω=sη_m has exactly the periods of c on arithmetic cycles.",
      "hypotheses": "Fix o in the cone (o=I in the application). Stokes for C¹ differential forms on affine simplices in the open convex cone. The homogeneous data and equivariance make the correction b left-invariant. Its coboundary vanishes after evaluation on a bar cycle with zero boundary.",
      "definitions": [
        "W_j is the integral of η_j(g₀,…,g_{m−j}) on the j-simplex with vertices A_{g_{m−j}}o,…,A_{g_m}o.",
        "B_j on g₀,…,g_{m−1} integrates Kη_j(g₀,…,g_{m−1−j}) on the j-simplex with vertices A_{g_{m−1−j}}o,…,A_{g_{m−1}}o.",
        "W₀=c. The computed telescoping signs obey s₀=1 and s_{j+1}=s_j(−1)^(m−j). Thus for this recurrence s_m=(−1)^(m(m+1)/2); sWhit_of requests only the resulting witness s=±1.",
        "The concrete Stokes proof writes the exterior derivative as an alternating sum of directional derivatives and integrates each along a coordinate interval. The upper face is re-expressed with its shifted base vertex."
