    {
      "id": "CFM-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The arithmetic partition supplies the growth and initial scalar invariance",
      "anchor": "inputs-cocycle-height",
      "statement": "At the selected arithmetic partition the moving frame of the resulting m-form has norm ≤C height^(am). One uniform exponent works in every matrix size N≥1, and the body of pf_GFin exhibits a=1. The form already has invariance under scalar tuples with equal absolute values.",
      "hypotheses": "The field for SPU is totally complex and fixed before choosing a. N and the smooth partition are chosen before the input cocycle is realized. The size of the derivative constant, finite overlaps and values of c on relevant finite tuples can depend on N and c. General SWhit takes an invariant nonnegative weight Ht supplied as height^a. Full scalar-tuple invariance is obtained in the next central-average step.",
      "definitions": [
        "The smooth partition generator is φ=ψ∘ret∘nf in pf_GFin. The normalized/retracted points have primal and dual lattice minima bounded below, so their arithmetic translates reach a compact region covered by the chosen bump.",
        "There is a finite set O of relative labels whose translated support closures meet. At a point with at least one active label γ₀ the others inject into O by γ↦γ₀⁻¹γ.",
        "If the moving derivatives of every weight are bounded by M, then the recurrence in claim yields C_{j+1}=|O|(j+1)C_j for the bound ‖η_j‖≤C_j M^j on the active tuples. Common left translation bounds the initial values of c on finitely many relative tuples.",
        "The height lower bound c₀>0 turns 1+ht into (1+c₀⁻¹)ht. Homogeneity under a common positive dilation of the Hermitian coordinates gives equal-modulus scalar invariance."
      ],
